<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tianma-Qucun site</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tianma-Qucun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tianma-Qucun site is a large archaeological site in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, between the villages of Tianma and Qucun near Houma. Excavations since the 1960s, and especially of the Beizhao cemetery from 1992, revealed the tombs of the early marquises of Jin and their consorts, with inscribed bronzes and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> pits. They confirmed that the early capital of the State of Jin lay there.</p></div>
